=================== PART 2: switch path contrast ===================
PIX/PXB = GPU and NIC under the same PCIe switch (switch-local peer-to-peer).
NODE    = GPU reaches the NIC via the root complex (does NOT do switch-local P2P).
If the switch's P2P handling is the fault, NODE should behave differently.

no NODE-distance 400 Gb/s rail found -- skipped

=================== PART 3: concurrency scaling ===================
N GPU/NIC pairs bidirectional at once. Per-pair rate constant => per-port limit.
Per-pair rate falling as N grows => shared switch resource saturating.

